WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.809
Geppetto carried his talking wood home carefully.

2
00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:06.405
Geppetto’s home was simple and clean.

3
00:00:06.406 --> 00:00:10.967
He had one large room with a bed, a table, his tools, and a stove.

4
00:00:10.968 --> 00:00:14.731
Although Geppetto worked hard, he did not have very much money.

5
00:00:14.732 --> 00:00:17.032
But he didn’t mind.

6
00:00:17.033 --> 00:00:21.737
"Now, where should I start?" he wondered aloud.

7
00:00:21.738 --> 00:00:24.315
"I’ve never made a boy before."

8
00:00:24.316 --> 00:00:26.077
"Start with the legs!

9
00:00:26.078 --> 00:00:29.826
That way I can run fast!" said the wood.

10
00:00:29.827 --> 00:00:35.868
"No, I think you had better have eyes first, so you don’t run into walls.

11
00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:41.095
I don’t want you to get hurt," Geppetto said.

12
00:00:41.096 --> 00:00:44.097
He was happy to be making his very own boy.

13
00:00:44.098 --> 00:00:49.034
He started first by carving out the face, and then he carved the eyes.

14
00:00:49.035 --> 00:00:55.335
As the wood looked more like a boy’s face, he became excited about what he and his boy could do together.

15
00:00:55.336 --> 00:00:58.954
What fun they would have!

16
00:00:58.955 --> 00:01:02.490
"There, your eyes look very smart.

17
00:01:02.491 --> 00:01:06.769
How well can you see?" Geppetto asked.

18
00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:10.071
"Oh, it’s terrible!" cried the wood.

19
00:01:10.072 --> 00:01:13.643
"What’s wrong?" asked Geppetto, worried.

20
00:01:13.644 --> 00:01:17.205
He thought maybe the wood was blind.

21
00:01:17.206 --> 00:01:19.430
"We are very poor!

22
00:01:19.431 --> 00:01:21.662
Look at this small room!

23
00:01:21.663 --> 00:01:25.795
I want to be rich, not poor," the wood said.

24
00:01:25.796 --> 00:01:28.574
Geppetto was sad that his boy was ashamed of his home.

25
00:01:28.575 --> 00:01:32.799
He promised himself that his boy would have whatever he needed.

26
00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:39.253
"I will carve out your ears next, so that you can hear and learn," Geppetto said.

27
00:01:39.254 --> 00:01:42.415
Geppetto worked carefully on the wood all through the day.

28
00:01:42.416 --> 00:01:46.735
He carved hair, a nose, and a smile before lunch.

29
00:01:46.736 --> 00:01:51.884
Then, he shared his first meal of bread and cheese with his boy.

30
00:01:51.885 --> 00:01:55.808
"You and I will have great fun together, boy,"

31
00:01:55.809 --> 00:01:57.969
said Geppetto as he ate his meal.

32
00:01:57.970 --> 00:02:01.851
He tore off some bread and put it into the boy’s mouth.

33
00:02:01.852 --> 00:02:04.787
"Only I shouldn’t call you 'boy'.

34
00:02:04.788 --> 00:02:09.929
You need a name. What should we name you?"

35
00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:17.198
"I know! My name can be Prince Edmund of the Great Woods," said the wood.

36
00:02:17.199 --> 00:02:21.180
He liked the name because it sounded big and important.

37
00:02:21.181 --> 00:02:25.068
"That is too big a name for such a small boy.

38
00:02:25.069 --> 00:02:29.650
Since you are made of pinewood, I will call you Pinocchio.

39
00:02:29.651 --> 00:02:32.215
What do you think?" asked Geppetto.

40
00:02:32.216 --> 00:02:35.647
He wanted to pick a name the boy would like.

41
00:02:35.648 --> 00:02:45.290
"Yes—Pinocchio. That sounds important, though it doesn’t sound as grand as Prince Edmund of the Great Woods.

42
00:02:45.291 --> 00:02:48.995
I think it will be fine," he agreed.

43
00:02:48.996 --> 00:02:52.868
"Wonderful! Pinocchio it is!

44
00:02:52.869 --> 00:02:58.321
To celebrate, I will carve your arms and legs so we can dance!"

45
00:02:58.322 --> 00:03:01.972
And Geppetto carved quickly.

46
00:03:01.973 --> 00:03:08.939
As soon as Geppetto finished carving Pinocchio’s feet, Pinocchio jumped to the floor and ran out of the front door.

47
00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:11.965
"Wait!" Geppetto called out.

48
00:03:11.966 --> 00:03:15.209
"Pinocchio, where are you going?"

49
00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:19.911
"I am off to find adventures!" Pinocchio called.

50
00:03:19.912 --> 00:03:23.347
"But, you don’t have any clothes on yet!

51
00:03:23.348 --> 00:03:26.103
You can’t run away if you are naked!

52
00:03:26.104 --> 00:03:30.803
Please, don’t leave!" Geppetto cried, as he ran after Pinocchio.

53
00:03:30.804 --> 00:03:35.799
Unfortunately, Geppetto forgot to leave his knife on the table.

54
00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:39.159
He was running after Pinocchio with his knife still in his hand!

55
00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:43.389
The neighbors thought he wanted to hurt Pinocchio, so they called for the police:

56
00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:47.163
"Police, police! Catch him!"

57
00:03:47.164 --> 00:03:53.318
One of the policemen was nearby, and he ran into the street just in time to catch Geppetto.

58
00:03:53.319 --> 00:03:56.455
He would not let Geppetto explain about Pinocchio.

59
00:03:56.456 --> 00:04:04.143
The policeman was scared of Geppetto’s knife, so he threw him in jail for the night.

